    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bdde4af_a03dec48",
        "filename": "telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ITelephony.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 604,
      "author": {
        "id": 1609802
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-18T19:33:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Indeed. All four options has its own Pros/Cons:\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1PXd3RDxWx3D9g8EBnfhR591FDnrC8aH8arHzCQL1l_I/edit#\n\nThe unified mutable parcelable does have a little mass to organize all info, but this is a typical usage of parcelable. We get benefits:\n1. A unified/symmetric ITelephony APIs to open/close channel\n2. Expendable for support more features\n3. Serve as a reusable containers for pass through process boundary (e.g. TelephonyRegister can re-use it to support the phone process crash case)\n4. No boilerplate logic to maintain",
      "parentUuid": "b5f3957e_00632e8e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 604,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 604,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "93f368561fe43cbd8862e97924146f6cf5759a3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "789900a9_4fdc7b4f",
        "filename": "telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ITelephony.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 604,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124543
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-23T03:57:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the open call doesn\u0027t use the channel ID (6/7 fields used), and then the close call only uses slot/sub + package + channel ID (3/7 fields used). I don\u0027t think there\u0027s really enough overlap here to reasonably say we need to use the same object for both open and close but I defer to a telephony reviewer here.",
      "parentUuid": "4bdde4af_a03dec48",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 604,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 604,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "93f368561fe43cbd8862e97924146f6cf5759a3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "427adde3_b6be95ea",
        "filename": "telephony/java/com/android/internal/telephony/ITelephony.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 604,
      "author": {
        "id": 1609802
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-23T17:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The 4 options in the doc explored multiple way on how to organize the input/output parameters:\n1. Keep all parameters separated (as it is) (Alternative 1)\n2. Put open parameters into a parcelable (manually constructed) but leave close parameters as is (Alternative 2)\n3. Use immutable AIDL parcelable to separate open/close requests(Alternative 3)\n4 Use mutable AIDL parcelable to organize both open/close parameters into a union request (Alternative 4)\n\nAgain, all options has Pros./Cons. but Alternative 4 seems be best suitable for our case without boilerplate.\n\nLet\u0027s check if telephony reviewers have any preference here.\nThanks",
      "parentUuid": "789900a9_4fdc7b4f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 604,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 604,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "93f368561fe43cbd8862e97924146f6cf5759a3c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
