        "id": 1609802
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-11-18T19:33:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "union does get support starting from Android 12, but the generated java look quite costy:\nhttps://paste.googleplex.com/4645269179203584\n\nThis is a bit too much (separate parcelabe with value/tag for the the union, a more level of reference...)\n\nWe can even organize the request in more hierarchy (e.g. separate open/close parameter). But it will generate more complicated data class.\n\nA flat parcelable is much simpler and easier to use. In the future, if the AIDL support get better and we get more complicated cases, may be we can try. For now, it looks not worthy it.",
